``

## INTERSECT (MySQL using INNER JOIN)

### 46. Find employees present in both tables.

```sql
SELECT c.*
FROM CurrentEmployees c
INNER JOIN FormerEmployees f
ON c.EmployeeID = f.EmployeeID;
```

### 47. Find common departments.

```sql
SELECT DISTINCT c.Department
FROM CurrentEmployees c
INNER JOIN FormerEmployees f
ON c.Department = f.Department;
```

### 48. Find customers present in both customer tables.

```sql
SELECT d.*
FROM DomesticCustomers d
INNER JOIN InternationalCustomers i
ON d.CustomerID = i.CustomerID;
```

### 49. Find common cities.

```sql
SELECT DISTINCT d.City
FROM DomesticCustomers d
INNER JOIN InternationalCustomers i
ON d.City = i.City;
```

### 50. Find common orders.

```sql
SELECT o.*
FROM OnlineOrders o
INNER JOIN StoreOrders s
ON o.OrderID = s.OrderID;
```

### 51. Find employee IDs common to both tables.

